<resources>

    <!-- How much of the display width the floating search card takes.

         100% means "leave the layout alone" — the card is match_parent inside its margins, which
         is the right shape on a phone, where the screen is barely wider than the card needs to be.

         A tablet in landscape is the case this exists for: the same card stretched across ~1160dp
         is a search field with most of a metre of empty space in it, and result rows whose icon
         and label sit alone at the far left. Three fifths, centred, keeps the card at roughly the
         proportions it has on a phone. Portrait on a tablet is left at full width — the screen is
         only as wide as a large phone's there, so the card is already in proportion.

         Read by QuickSearchActivity.positionCard. -->
    <fraction name="quick_search_card_width">100%</fraction>

</resources>
